7592186045417] [17592186096886 #edb/ref 1044 #edb/ref 17592186045463 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096886 #edb/ref 1045 "Describing the Position Vector of a Point Using Known Vectors" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096886 #edb/ref 1046 #edb/ref 17592186097486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096886 #edb/ref 1049 #edb/ref 17592186048780 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186096886 #edb/ref 1053 #uuid "90bcccea-5782-59d1-a524-d6852abe26cd" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097486 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186362445 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097486 #edb/ref 1061 661397 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097486 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e10b4911-140a-5838-a16e-13feb12fba7b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097486 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186097837 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097487 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186097488 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097487 #edb/ref 1061 661408 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097487 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "e9410dda-1b4e-5dca-b7ed-64fdcc297e4e" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097487 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096652 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097488 #edb/ref 1061 661411 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097488 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "eb2bab86-218f-5b3a-9a4e-b0b3872ba6db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097488 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096653 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097564 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186362452 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097564 #edb/ref 1061 661399 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097564 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "74a3f281-5081-51cb-a589-0b5531ea612f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097564 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186096701 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097837 #edb/ref 1064 "Given a fixed **origin** in the plane (often denoted ![](images/75/7502527c010624a805906c12d7a6e94363988e41b1c40771a4cc4fc82900e083.svg)), and another point ![](images/42/42193b6382254991fb9c053ead9edd0631767155ea51d8a8551cfc4fc734340e.svg) the vector ![](images/20/20edf7e26e0b35148bf8ff1e9b52c38e5b6672ae0462a8c2e218e1c0456bae07.svg) is called the **position vector** of the point ![](images/ed/ed6dc1fd057e3dd2207c735a562bf4db22b72d1a9380651607439f00c0440725.svg)\n\nSo, the position vector tells us how to move from the origin to the point.\n\nFor example, suppose ![](images/4f/4f9204dcee76e03f03dc64827bf810327c9b2b981a0aee5a10c7f80ca98f4d5d.svg) and ![](images/41/412bd151cdf5602575028591e2f87d9a7e0328aa6b18dccb6459e7041a5d9b9c.svg) How can we find the position vector ![](images/20/20edf7e26e0b35148bf8ff1e9b52c38e5b6672ae0462a8c2e218e1c0456bae07.svg) in terms of ![](images/52/527e0abeb684dd24d8c92e45425542080c4c9493b9460bb89753fef3226c1f92.svg) and ![](images/c5/c5d2e1827ba6a11504655381514c15ce7eba142e62bf8dca3a10d12eef9d7861.svg)\n\n![](images/e6/e61003fb62534b04cfbbac07a64e61f6c16e2d464eb35bc5b98654b0603b24db.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, we can trace a path from ![](images/75/7502527c010624a805906c12d7a6e94363988e41b1c40771a4cc4fc82900e083.svg) to ![](images/46/46833dd7644e5c60bb4525fe4e7649a99752b26096331755a4b44c2abe183f11.svg) by first moving from ![](images/75/7502527c010624a805906c12d7a6e94363988e41b1c40771a4cc4fc82900e083.svg) to ![](images/c2/c2c85081d1f89d74b8ebb2761496d211d7052193809b7864e7983437f5d0b80f.svg) and then from ![](images/32/3207697e43e4f88223ad85c16964c3103a50c0c999a4ca14417695158d45526b.svg) to ![](images/ed/ed6dc1fd057e3dd2207c735a562bf4db22b72d1a9380651607439f00c0440725.svg) Therefore,\n![](images/ac/ac96d55fd0d74cf5fd24f1f1a96beb3865bc70bc45d17be5aad209c5adb1be6d.svg)\n\nSince ![](images/4f/4f9204dcee76e03f03dc64827bf810327c9b2b981a0aee5a10c7f80ca98f4d5d.svg) and ![](images/e2/e283cb6e7ab325c89dd652abd93ff1382b714462887d8839dfed8769693cc7a7.svg) we get\n![](images/e1/e1bde038ef63f77c3ecc5357b49999c96dd6d331aa7455fcdd1935b1f3eb8261.svg)\n\nSo, to find a position vector, we can trace a convenient path from the origin to the point and add the vectors along that path." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186097837 #edb/ref 1065 2910 #edb/ref 1